`onSelectPackage` is currently wired to `setSelectedPackage`, which updates local state but does not update the router URL. With URL-param routing (`/$package/...`), this can leave the UI state and URL out of sync (and will also be overwritten by the `/$package` param-sync effect). Prefer navigating to the selected package route (e.g., `navigate({ to: '/$package', params: { package: pkgId } })` or `navigate({ to: `/${pkgId}` })`) and derive `selectedPackage` from the URL.
```suggestion
import { createFileRoute, useNavigate } from '@tanstack/react-router';
import { AppSidebar } from '../components/app-sidebar';
import { SiteHeader } from '@/components/site-header';
import { DeveloperOverview } from '../components/DeveloperOverview';
import { usePackages } from '../hooks/usePackages';

function IndexComponent() {
  const navigate = useNavigate();
  const { packages, selectedPackage } = usePackages();

  return (
    <>
      <AppSidebar
        packages={packages}
        selectedPackage={selectedPackage}
        onSelectPackage={(packageId) =>
          navigate({
            to: '/$package',
            params: { package: packageId },
          })
        }
```

